By some minor miracle (and help from spoilers and r.g.r.n.), Heidi
the Lawful Drarven Valkyrie is still alive and kicking.  She
chased Lord Surtur up a few levels before hacking him to bits with
the rustproof +7 Mjollnir (now blessed, too!) and absconding with
the Quest Goodies(tm).  She's cleaned out the mines, too.

A bit of alchemy and magic-markering later, the executive summary
looks like this:

    intrinsic cold, fire, and poison resistance
    extrinsic reflection (from pushing boulders into pits)
    extrinsic invisibility (from a ring)
    (no foo of enlightenment to be sure, though)

    12 blessed +3 elven daggers
    the blessed rustproof +7 Mjollnir (wielded expertly)
    the blessed rustproof -3 Excalibur (engraving accident)
    a blessed +1 elven mithril-coat (found it that way)
    an uncursed fireproof +3 small shield
    a blessed +5 orcish helm (found it that way!)
    a blessed +4 cloak of protection
    a blessed +4 Hawaiian shirt
    an uncursed +4 pair of low boots (found them that way!)
    an uncursed +0 pair of gauntlets of power

    one uncursed wax candle

Str 25 (18/68 under those gloves), Dex 19, Con 20, Int 15, Wis 16,
Cha 13.

190 HP, AC -23 (I don't know how she lost her 5 points of divine
protection), 180024 experience.  Wishless by circumstance, not by
choice.

As a Dwarf, can she eat an Elf for sleep resistance without
incurring any penalties?

Less useful:

    piles of wands and un-id'd rings with un-obvious effects
    an almost dried magic marker
    a bunch of healing potions and teleportation scrolls
    enough valuable gems to choke several unicorns

Level 24 is Medusa's Island.  Unfortuately, there's nary a source
of levitation (rings, potions, boots, or otherwise) to be had.  No
foo of polymorph, wands of wishing, or smoky potions, either.

So how can Heidi get to Medusa?  She has a couple of wands of cold
(charges unknown); can she freeze a path and walk across that?  Is
there something else we're missing?

OTOH, now that I think about it, is digging down and then coming
back up a better solution?

This is as far as I've ever gotten; I'd hate to screw it up now.

On a different note, there are a couple of peaceful Aleax's and a
peaceful Fire Giant a few levels up.  Are either of those worth a
scroll of taming, or should she hold out for something better or
an emergency?

